Repair the PatternDSL v0.2 candidate for grammar counted_grid. Preserve this task brief: Training v1 variant 3: Create an original geometric tile inspired by Gamosa red-on-white border and motif band. Use abstract motif guidance from supplementary-weft motifs (flowers, diamonds, cross borders, stylised birds) built block-by-block from graph paper where each block equals one or; distribute it with close-spaced spacing and a clear center. Avoid named sacred or identity-specific symbols. Use this palette order: #FAF8F2, #C41E3A, #1E5AA8. Treat the palette as approximate color guidance..
GRAMMAR_RULES: Quantize every mark to the host cell grid. Set constraints.cell_size to the host value. Do not add a top-level grid or counted_grid field; cell_size belongs only in constraints. Use full host-sized cells only, with each filled cell uniform within every layer. Do not use dots, diamonds, or diagonal motifs; use axis-aligned rectangles whose edges align exactly to cell boundaries. For each rectangle, both center minus half its size and center plus half its size must be multiples of cell_size on both axes; its width and height must be whole cell multiples.

LAYER_AND_MOTIF_SCHEMA: Layers use the exact keys "id", "colour_index", "anchor", "motifs". A dot motif is {"kind": "dot", "center": [x, y], "radius": r}; diamond uses the same fields, rectangle uses {"kind": "rectangle", "center": [x, y], "size": [w, h]}, line uses {"kind": "line", "points": [[x1, y1], [x2, y2]], "stroke": n}, and polygon uses {"kind": "polygon", "points": [[x1, y1], [x2, y2], [x3, y3]]}. Never use name, dots, type, cx, or centre as field names. The root object has only schema_version, grammar, tradition_id, title, tile, palette, background_index, layers, constraints, kolam, and jaali as applicable. tile must be an object with width, height, wrap_x, wrap_y; palette has 1..6 colours; layers has 1..4 objects; each layer id is a string and motifs is an array. Never use integer layer ids, a tile array, or extra fields.
